#   Ghent and corporate: not converted: both locations and location groups: how ZIA combines them is not known; the source of the rule is in zone Branch-Ghent, HQ-Brussels, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind Branch-Ghent, HQ-Brussels with --zone-network; the destination of the rule is in zone
#   Web for all: the source of the rule is in zone HQ-Brussels, Branch-Ghent, HQ-Servers, Guest-WiFi, road-warrior, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind HQ-Brussels, Branch-Ghent, Guest-WiFi, road-warrior with --zone-network; the destination of the rule is in zone internet, and a rule o
#   Guest ICMP: the source of the rule is in zone Guest-WiFi, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind Guest-WiFi with --zone-network; the destination of the rule is in zone internet, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind internet with --zone-network

echo 'Done. Associate the policy with the network when you are ready; until then nothing changes.' >&2
